  "description": {
   "text": "Shapechange\n(Alteration)\n\nLevel: 9\nRange: 0\nDuration: 6 turns\nCasting Time: 9\nArea of Effect: The caster\nSaving Throw: None\n\nWith this spell the wizard can take the shape of six powerful creatures. Each form, and the wizard's natural form, becomes a special ability for the duration: the wizard can change between them at any time and as often as <PRO_HESHE> wishes. In another form the wizard keeps <PRO_HISHER> mind and Hit Points but takes the body of the creature: its Strength, Dexterity, base Armor Class, THAC0, attacks and natural protections; the bonus for a high Dexterity still counts. The wizard can cast spells and use items in every form except the iron golem and the greater basilisk. When the spell ends, the wizard returns to <PRO_HISHER> natural form.\n\nMind Flayer: 4 attacks per round that drain Intelligence; Magic Resistance 90%, 50% physical resistance; Psionic Blast stuns.\nIron Golem: Strength 24, 4d10 crushing as a +4 weapon; Magic Resistance 100%, immune to the elements and to weapons below +3; Gas Cloud every 3 rounds.\nGiant Troll: Strength 22, 3 attacks per round; regenerates about 2 Hit Points a second.\nMarilith: 5 attacks per round, base Armor Class -6; Magic Resistance 85%, immune to fire and electricity; Teleport.\nGreater Basilisk: 3 poisonous attacks per round; Petrifying Gaze.\nInvisible Stalker: improved-invisible every round; 80% resistance to missiles.",
   "old": 26362
